          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An attic fan is not the upgrade most houses need. Air sealing the ceiling, adding insulation and fixing blocked soffit intake will do more for comfort and bills in an air-conditioned home, and if you want cooler rooms in a climate with cool evenings, a whole house fan is the better tool.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If an attic fan suits your house, buy the QuietCool AFG SMT ES-3.0 for a gable or the AFR SMT ES-2.0 for a hip roof, give it the intake it needs, set the thermostat high and switch the humidistat off in winter. For garages and sheds, a Remington solar fan is the simplest answer.
          </p>
